background_video_name": "Minecraft jumping circuit", "background_music_name": "Music dj quads", "facts_type": "facts about sleeping", "script": "Fascinating facts about sleeping. Dolphins sleep with one eye open and one brain hemisphere at a time, allowing them to stay alert while resting. Humans can take up to 14 minutes longer to fall asleep when using electronic devices before bed. In Japan, it\u2019s socially acceptable to sleep on the job\u2014it\u2019s seen as a sign of hard work and dedication. Sleep talkers can produce entire conversations, but the content is rarely remembered. The record for the longest time without sleep is 11 days, held by a high school student in 1965.", "temp_audio_path": ".editing_assets/facts_shorts_assets/aba2d8277f544287944dae06/temp_audio_path.wav", "audio_path": ".editing_assets/facts_shorts_assets/aba2d8277f544287944dae06/audio_voice.wav", "timed_captions": [[[0.2, 0.7], "Fascinating"], [[0.7, 1.32], "facts about"], [[1.32, 1.76], "sleeping."], [[2.64, 3.44], "Dolphins sleep"], [[3.44, 4.04], "with one eye"], [[4.04, 4.7], "open and one"], [[4.7, 4.96], "brain"], [[4.96, 5.74], "hemisphere at a"], [[5.74, 6.48], "time, allowing"], [[6.48, 7.1], "them to stay"], [[7.1, 7.62], "alert while"], [[7.62, 9.4], "resting. Humans"], [[9.4, 10.12], "can take up to"], [[10.12, 10.74], "14 minutes"], [[10.74, 11.47], "longer to fall"], [[11.47, 12.1], "asleep when"], [[12.1, 12.4], "using"], [[12.4, 12.94], "electronic"], [[12.94, 13.86], "devices before"], [[13.86, 15.26], "bed. In"], [[15.26, 16.0], "Japan, it's"], [[16.0, 16.32], "socially"], [[16.32, 17.1], "acceptable to"], [[17.1, 17.66], "sleep on the"], [[17.66, 18.52], "job, it's seen"], [[18.52, 19.28], "as a sign of"], [[19.28, 19.96], "hard work and"], [[19.96, 20.42], "dedication."], [[21.32, 22.26], "Sleep talkers"], [[22.26, 22.74], "can produce"], [[22.74, 23.15], "entire"], [[23.15, 23.86], "conversations,"], [[24.24, 24.78], "but the content"], [[24.78, 25.32], "is really"]