%2C136%2C160%2C242%2C243%2C244%2C247%2C278%2C298%2C299%2C302%2C303&source=youtube&requiressl=yes&xpc=EgVo2aDSNQ%3D%3D&met=1746088634%2C&mh=Rg&mm=31%2C26&mn=sn-42u-i5ol6%2Csn-ogul7n7s&ms=au%2Conr&mv=m&mvi=1&pl=24&rms=au%2Cau&initcwndbps=3111250&bui=AecWEAatAFNr0kdJAJk68lzHH43dWztLasbBM9KtW01EzWswcLEgv7t3YQYsINSvrJADsAajWhLENSQL&vprv=1&svpuc=1&mime=video%2Fwebm&ns=JYrjXVJoGOTH_cwsbImzRu4Q&rqh=1&gir=yes&clen=257785144&dur=575.141&lmt=1640042918418010&mt=1746088168&fvip=5&keepalive=yes&lmw=1&c=TVHTML5&sefc=1&txp=5316224&n=X01AJ0aZoCN_Cg&sparams=expire%2Cei%2Cip%2Cid%2Caitags%2Csource%2Crequiressl%2Cxpc%2Cbui%2Cvprv%2Csvpuc%2Cmime%2Cns%2Crqh%2Cgir%2Cclen%2Cdur%2Clmt&sig=AJfQdSswRQIgH_HIxuD-Qei3yXujWk4cRSRce9jwvjiY0glJxkERitgCIQDM6PbwWeHobN_YvNl1xcH4iDBUimVmqsdFeWcKjuInyQ%3D%3D&lsparams=met%2Cmh%2Cmm%2Cmn%2Cms%2Cmv%2Cmvi%2Cpl%2Crms%2Cinitcwndbps&lsig=ACuhMU0wRAIgCwa9orUFLOQ288xe7EsfIidoBF5Ww5CJuChch8X6DOYCIA4W5qm1bI68bEaBUgpbabzShXBbWkWU2fn7HmHyy2QH", "background_video_duration": 575.141, "voiceover_duration": 33.648, "background_trimmed": ".editing_assets/facts_shorts_assets/aba2d8277f544287944dae06/clipped_background.mp4", "video_path": "videos/2025-05-01_15-39-47 -  5 Fascinating Facts About Sleep You Never Knew.mp4", "yt_title": "\ud83d\ude0d 5 Fascinating Facts About Sleep You Never Knew", "yt_description": "Did you know dolphins sleep with one eye open? Discover more sleep facts! #SleepFacts #DidYouKnow"}, "3": {"_id": "5f3a5c7cb2784f818b42185f", "content_type": "general_video", "ready_to_upload": true, "last_completed_step": 10, "language": "English", "script": "Did you know that the human brain is about 2% of the body's weight but uses about 20% of its energy? It contains around 86 billion neurons, and each one can connect to thousands of others, creating a complex network that enables us to think, feel, and move. Despite its incredible power, the brain can only store about 1 to 2 gigabytes of conscious memories. Interestingly, the brain generates about 70,000 thoughts a day, and it can grow new neurons throughout your life, a process called neurogenesis. The brain also has its own unique way of recycling energy, and it does this while we sleep, which is why a good night\u2019s rest is so important for cognitive function. Lastly, the brain can process images that the eye sees in just 13 milliseconds, making it one of the fastest and most efficient processors in the world.", "format_vertical": true, "temp_audio_path": ".editing_assets/general_video_assets/5f3a5c7cb2784f818b42185f/temp_audio_path.wav", "audio_path": ".editing_assets/general_video_assets/5f3a5c7cb2784f818b42185f/temp_audio_path.wav", "timed_captions": [[[0.18, 0.56], "Did you know"], [[0.56, 1.14], "that the human"], [[1.14, 1.98], "brain is about"], [[1.98, 2.86], "2% of the"], [[2.86, 3.42], "body's weight"], [[3.42, 4.22], "but uses about"], [[4.22, 5.14], "20% of its"], [[5.14, 6.62], "energy? It"], [[6.62, 7.3], "contains around"], [[7.3, 8.2], "86 billion"], [[8.2, 8.9], "neurons and"], [[8.9, 9.58], "each one can"], [[9.58, 10.08], "connect to"], [[10.08, 10.6], "thousands of"], [[10.6, 10.9], "others,"], [[11.1, 11.64], "creating a"], [[11.64, 12.44], "complex network"], [[12.44, 13.26], "that enables us"], [[13.26, 13.42], "to"], [[13.42, 13.66], "think,"], [[13.86, 14.44], "feel, and"], [[14.44, 16.04], "move. Despite"], [[16.04, 16.68], "its incredible"], [[16.68, 17.4], "power, the"], [[17.4, 18.1], "brain can only"], [[18.1, 18.9], "store about one"], [[18.9, 19.28], "to two"], [[19.28, 19.9], "gigabytes of"], [[19.9, 20.01], "conscious"], [[20.01, 20.58], "memories."], [[21.08, 22.18], "Interestingly,"], [[22.54, 22.84], "the brain"], [[22.84, 23.58], "generates about"], [[23.58, 24.6], "70,000 thoughts"], [[24.6, 25.44], "a day and it"], [[25.44, 25.8], "can grow"], [[25.8, 26.14], "neurons"], [[26.14, 26.84], "throughout your"], [[26.84, 27.82], "life, a process"], [[27.82, 28.14], "called"], [[28.14, 28.9], "neurogenesis."], [[30.02, 30.74], "T