language": "English", "auto_music": true, "background_music_name": "", "script": "Did you know that the feeling of love is actually a chemical reaction in your brain? When you fall in love, your body releases hormones like dopamine, oxytocin, and serotonin. These chemicals create feelings of pleasure, attachment, and well-being. Interestingly, the brain\u2019s reward system is more active when you're in love than when you're using drugs like cocaine! Love also has some surprising benefits. It can reduce stress, boost your immune system, and even help you live longer. So, the next time you feel that special connection, remember it\u2019s not just a feeling\u2014it\u2019s a powerful biological process that\u2019s essential to our well-being.", "format_vertical": true, "temp_audio_path": ".editing_assets/general_video_assets/262bdc926edd4b498d8fb376/temp_audio_path.wav", "audio_path": ".editing_assets/general_video_assets/262bdc926edd4b498d8fb376/temp_audio_path.wav", "timed_captions": [[[0.18, 0.58], "Did you know"], [[0.58, 0.86], "that the"], [[0.86, 1.48], "feeling of love"], [[1.48, 2.2], "is actually a"], [[2.2, 2.48], "chemical"], [[2.48, 3.16], "reaction in"], [[3.16, 3.28], "your"], [[3.28, 4.9], "brain? When you"], [[4.9, 5.26], "fall in"], [[5.26, 6.08], "love, your body"], [[6.08, 6.5], "releases"], [[6.5, 7.2], "hormones like"], [[7.2, 7.62], "dopamine,"], [[7.84, 8.88], "oxytocin, and"], [[8.88, 9.52], "serotonin."], [[9.76, 11.08], "These chemicals"], [[11.08, 11.86], "create feelings"], [[11.86, 12.08], "of"], [[12.08, 12.42], "pleasure,"], [[12.48, 13.46], "attachment, and"], [[13.46, 13.88], "well-being."], [[14.2, 15.32], "Interestingly,"], [[15.68, 16.14], "the brain's"], [[16.14, 16.78], "reward system"], [[16.78, 17.58], "is more active"], [[17.58, 18.28], "when you're in"], [[18.28, 18.9], "love than when"], [[18.9, 19.34], "you're using"], [[19.34, 19.92], "drugs like"], [[19.92, 21.62], "cocaine. Love"], [[21.62, 22.4], "also has some"], [[22.4