#CatLovers #FascinatingFacts"}, "19": {"_id": "2129779b7ab642168561a09c", "content_type": "general_video", "ready_to_upload": true, "last_completed_step": 10, "language": "English", "auto_music": false, "background_music_name": "Blue yungkai", "script": "Did you know that the observable universe is estimated to be about 93 billion light-years in diameter? That means the light from the farthest objects we can see has been traveling to us for over 13.8 billion years. It's a mind-boggling scale, filled with trillions of galaxies, each containing billions of stars. And yet, despite its vastness, we\u2019re still discovering new wonders within it. From supermassive black holes to mysterious dark matter, the universe continues to fascinate and challenge our understanding. Each discovery brings us a step closer to unraveling the secrets of our cosmic home.", "format_vertical": true, "temp_audio_path": ".editing_assets/general_video_assets/2129779b7ab642168561a09c/temp_audio_path.wav", "audio_path": ".editing_assets/general_video_assets/2129779b7ab642168561a09c/temp_audio_path.wav", "timed_captions": [[[0.18, 0.56], "Did you know"], [[0.56, 0.9], "that the"], [[0.9, 1.4], "observable"], [[1.4, 2.04], "universe is"], [[2.04, 2.9], "estimated to be"], [[2.9, 3.6], "about 93"], [[3.6, 4.24], "billion light"], [[4.24, 4.66], "years in"], [[4.66, 6.3], "diameter? That"], [[6.3, 6.94], "means the light"], [[6.94, 7.3], "from the"], [[7.3, 7.7], "farthest"], [[7.7, 8.44], "objects we can"], [[8.44, 9.06], "see has been"], [[9.06, 9.82], "traveling to us"], [[9.82, 11.2], "for over 13.8"], [[11.2, 11.54], "billion"], [[11.54, 13.18], "years. It's a"], [[13.18, 13.66], "mind-bubbling"], [[13.66, 14.5], "scale, filled"], [[14.5, 15.1], "with trillions"], [[15.1, 15.32], "of"], [[15.32, 16.22], "galaxies, each"], [[16.22, 16.6], "containing"], [[16.6, 17.24], "billions of"], [[17.24, 18.82], "stars. And"], [[18.82, 19.52], "yet, despite"], [[19.52, 19.78], "its"], [[19.78, 20.52], "va